node_modules/

# The signing key and its password. Losing this file means never being able to
# ship an update that installs over an existing install -- Android identifies an
# app by package name *plus* signing key, so a rebuild with a new keystore is a
# different app to the OS. Back it up somewhere outside the repo.
keystore/

# The whole native project is generated: `npx cap add android` scaffolds it and
# `setup-android.sh` applies everything this project needs on top. Committing it
# would mean the flavours, the Kotlin plugin and the plugin registrars existed in
# two places -- android-overlay/ and android/ -- and the two would drift, with the
# copy that actually builds being the one nobody edits.
#
# Capacitor's own docs suggest committing it. The trade is deliberate, and it is
# only defensible because CI regenerates it from scratch on every run and then
# asserts the permission separation held.
android/


